thread:
maya: Quick FYI. Found a parity bug between SDKs: Python raises typed exceptions with .code and .status, but our Node sample got an opaque Error with message "permission denied" and no code. Sample apps that branch on err.code break.
alex: Yikes. Where did you hit this? Hosted or Dedicated?
maya: Hosted, embeddings call from the node quickstart with an expired token vs missing scope. Python handled it fine, JS did not.
samir: On the backend we definitely send structured body {code, message, retry_hint} but a few gateway proxies have been flattening or dropping fields for non-JSON content-types. That explains stray Error.message.
alex: Proposed SDK contract: every SDK should expose error.status (number), error.code (canonical string), error.message (human), and error.retry_hint (one of none, retry-after, idempotent-backoff). SDKs should also export typed classes (ApiError, AuthError, RetryableError) to make handling ergonomic.
julia-docs: I can draft a small snippet for onboarding that recommends robust checks. Example I want to add to docs:
```js
try {
  await client.embeddings.create({ input: ... })
} catch (err) {
  // prefer canonical fields when present
  if (err.code === 'unauthenticated' || err.status === 401) {
    // trigger reauth flow
  } else if (err.code === 'permission_denied' || err.status === 403) {
    // show link to permission docs in console
  } else if (err.retry_hint === 'retry-after') {
    // read err.headers['retry-after'] and retry after indicated time
  } else if (err.retry_hint === 'idempotent-backoff' || err.status >= 500) {
    // exponential backoff retry
  } else {
    // generic error UI
  }
}
```
maya: Also include a tiny backoff util and example parsing of Retry-After header. A lot of customers implement naive retry loops.
alex: I'll open a JS SDK PR to normalize gateway responses into our error model. Plan: if gateway response body is missing fields, map status->code using a canonical map, and populate retry_hint from headers or status. Add unit tests that simulate flattened gateway responses.
samir: I'll audit internal proxies and ensure they preserve the structured JSON body for API errors. If not possible, server will add fallback mapping before the response leaves the control plane.
devex-bot: Pinned resource: https://internal.redwood/docs/errors#canonical-shape 1. Use it as single source of truth for SDKs.
maya: One more question: should SDKs expose a boolean err.isTransient? Could be useful for sample apps instead of checking status codes.
alex: err.isTransient would be handy. We can compute it from retry_hint and status. Add to SDK contract: isTransient: stringified boolean.
julia-docs: I'll update onboarding samples, add a small troubleshooting section for common 401 vs 403 UX, and include migration notes for older SDKs.
maya: Great. Checklist: (1) alex - JS SDK PR to add ApiError/AuthError, map fields, tests (ETA 24h), (2) samir - proxy audit + server fallback mapping, (3) julia-docs - add snippets + backoff util and docs update. Ping here when each step is done.
alex: Starting PR now, will tag reviewers and include test matrix.
samir: I'll post audit findings in #eng-infra tomorrow.
